  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Show that $y=Ae^{-2x}+Be^{-3x}$ satisfies the differential equation $y''+5y'+6y=0$ for any real values of $A$ and $B$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y''+5y'+6y=0$.\n\nAfter substitution, the coefficients of $Ae^{-2x}$ and $Be^{-3x}$ are both zero.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*} y'&=-2Ae^{-2x}-3Be^{-3x}\\\\ y''&=4Ae^{-2x}+9Be^{-3x}\\\\ y''+5y'+6y&=(4Ae^{-2x}+9Be^{-3x})+5(-2Ae^{-2x}-3Be^{-3x})+6(Ae^{-2x}+Be^{-3x})\\\\ y''+5y'+6y&=(4-10+6)Ae^{-2x}+(9-15+6)Be^{-3x}\\\\ y''+5y'+6y&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 21
  },
